WEBVTT

00:00:53.053 --> 00:00:54.429
It's alive.

00:00:54.512 --> 00:00:57.807
It's alive. it's alive!

00:01:13.281 --> 00:01:15.700
There he is!
Hit it again!

00:01:25.502 --> 00:01:26.753
Success!

00:01:27.587 --> 00:01:29.422
Count, it's just you.

00:01:29.798 --> 00:01:33.051
I was beginning to
lose faith, Victor.

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:39.015
A pity your moment of
triumph is being spoiled

00:01:39.098 --> 00:01:41.601
over a little thing
like grave robbery.

00:01:41.684 --> 00:01:43.103
Yes.

00:01:44.062 --> 00:01:46.022
I must escape this place.

00:01:46.314 --> 00:01:48.817
Where are you going
to run, Victor?

00:01:50.193 --> 00:01:54.697
Your peculiar experiments
have made you unwelcome

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:57.200
in most of the civilized world.

00:01:57.325 --> 00:02:01.121
I'll take him away, far away,
where no one will ever find him.

00:02:01.412 --> 00:02:02.997
No, Victor.

00:02:03.081 --> 00:02:06.459
The time has come for me
to take command of him.

00:02:07.377 --> 00:02:08.795
What are you saying?

00:02:08.878 --> 00:02:11.756
Why do you think I brought you here?
Gave you this castle?

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:13.132
Equipped your laboratory?

00:02:13.216 --> 00:02:14.551
You said...

00:02:15.051 --> 00:02:17.137
You said you
believed in my work.

00:02:17.220 --> 00:02:18.721
And I do.

00:02:19.222 --> 00:02:23.643
But now that it is,
as you yourself have said,

00:02:23.726 --> 00:02:27.272
a triumph of science

00:02:27.981 --> 00:02:29.607
over God,

00:02:32.527 --> 00:02:36.114
it must now serve my purpose.

00:02:39.742 --> 00:02:41.327
What purpose?

00:02:53.965 --> 00:02:55.258
Good God!

00:02:55.967 --> 00:02:59.178
I would kill myself before
helping in such a task.

00:02:59.596 --> 00:03:02.932
Feel free. I don't actually
need you anymore, Victor.

00:03:03.141 --> 00:03:04.809
I just need him.

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:07.186
He is the key.

00:03:08.021 --> 00:03:11.190
I could never allow him
to be used for such evil.

00:03:11.691 --> 00:03:12.942
I could.

00:03:13.776 --> 00:03:16.863
In fact, my brides
are insisting upon it.

00:03:20.366 --> 00:03:22.535
Igor, help me!

00:03:22.619 --> 00:03:25.663
You have been
so kind to me, Doctor,

00:03:26.164 --> 00:03:28.458
caring, thoughtful.

00:03:28.625 --> 00:03:31.169
But he pays me.

00:03:35.214 --> 00:03:36.549
Stay back.

00:03:36.716 --> 00:03:39.177
You can't kill me, Victor.

00:03:42.889 --> 00:03:43.890
Ah!

00:03:45.808 --> 00:03:47.477
I'm already dead.

00:04:45.618 --> 00:04:47.870
Look, it's headed
for the windmill!

00:04:47.954 --> 00:04:49.539
Come on!

00:05:32.957 --> 00:05:35.752
Burn it!
Burn it down!

00:06:06.949 --> 00:06:08.951
Why?

00:06:19.796 --> 00:06:22.924
Why?

00:06:41.317 --> 00:06:42.610
Vampires.

00:06:42.819 --> 00:06:43.903
Run for your lives!

00:06:44.028 --> 00:06:45.488
Vampires!

00:07:06.717 --> 00:07:07.969
Father.

00:09:22.478 --> 00:09:23.729
Evening.

00:09:24.063 --> 00:09:27.942
You're a big one.
You'll be hard to digest.

00:09:29.235 --> 00:09:31.570
I'd hate to be such a nuisance.

00:09:39.579 --> 00:09:41.664
I missed you in London.

00:09:41.747 --> 00:09:45.584
No, you bloody did
not! You got me good.

00:09:45.918 --> 00:09:48.462
Dr. Jekyll, you're wanted by the
Knights of the Holy Order...

00:09:48.546 --> 00:09:49.839
it's Mr. Hyde now.

00:09:49.922 --> 00:09:52.675
...for the murder of
12 men, six women, four...

00:09:52.758 --> 00:09:57.680
Children, three goats, and a
rather nasty massacre of poultry!

00:09:58.431 --> 00:10:01.851
So you're
the great Van Helsing.

00:10:07.523 --> 00:10:10.318
We all have our
little problems.

00:10:12.695 --> 00:10:15.031
My superiors would like
for me to take you alive

00:10:15.114 --> 00:10:17.700
so that they may extricate
your better half.

00:10:17.867 --> 00:10:20.328
I bet they bloody would.

00:10:20.745 --> 00:10:24.248
Personally, I'd rather just
kill you and call it a day.

00:10:24.373 --> 00:10:26.000
But let's make it your
decision, shall we?

00:10:48.022 --> 00:10:50.399
Here I come,

00:10:50.483 --> 00:10:52.735
ready or not!

00:11:25.935 --> 00:11:27.978
I'll bet that's upsetting.

00:11:39.281 --> 00:11:40.866
Come here.

00:11:43.077 --> 00:11:47.915
I think you'll find the view
over here rather spectacular.

00:11:52.378 --> 00:11:54.463
It's been
a pleasure knowing you.

00:11:54.547 --> 00:11:56.006
Au revoir!

00:12:15.276 --> 00:12:16.444
Oh, no.

00:12:49.727 --> 00:12:51.479
May he rest in peace.

00:13:34.605 --> 00:13:35.856
Bless me, Father, for I have...

00:13:35.940 --> 00:13:39.610
Sinned. Yes, I know.
You're very good at that.

00:13:39.693 --> 00:13:41.654
You shattered the Rose Window.

00:13:41.737 --> 00:13:44.490
Not to split hairs, sir, but Mr.
Hyde did the shattering.

00:13:44.573 --> 00:13:48.202
13th century.
Over 600 years old.

00:13:49.078 --> 00:13:51.580
We are the last
defense against evil.

00:13:51.705 --> 00:13:55.125
An evil that the rest of mankind
has no idea even exists.

00:13:55.209 --> 00:13:59.797
To you, these monsters are just
evil beings to be vanquished.

00:14:01.715 --> 00:14:03.467
I'm the one standing
there when they die

00:14:03.551 --> 00:14:05.386
and become
the men they once were.

00:14:05.469 --> 00:14:09.014
For you, my good son, this
is all a test of faith.

00:14:09.431 --> 00:14:12.977
And now, we need
you to go to the East.

00:14:13.727 --> 00:14:16.230
To the far side of Romania.

00:14:17.106 --> 00:14:18.649
An accursed land

00:14:18.732 --> 00:14:21.735
terrorized by all sorts
of nightmarish creatures.

00:14:21.902 --> 00:14:25.155
Lorded over by
a certain Count Dracula.

00:14:25.739 --> 00:14:26.782
Dracula?

00:14:26.866 --> 00:14:27.908
Yes.

00:14:28.242 --> 00:14:30.953
You've never faced
one like this before.

00:14:31.912 --> 00:14:35.332
Our story begins 450 years ago

00:14:35.416 --> 00:14:39.169
when a Transylvanian knight,
named Valerious the Elder,

00:14:39.253 --> 00:14:42.756
promised God that his family would
never rest nor enter heaven

00:14:42.840 --> 00:14:45.885
until they vanquished
Dracula from their land.

00:14:46.427 --> 00:14:48.387
They have not succeeded

00:14:48.971 --> 00:14:51.515
and they are
running out of family.

00:14:52.433 --> 00:14:56.729
His descendant Boris Valerious,
King of the Gypsies.

00:14:59.148 --> 00:15:02.860
Valerious the Elder left
this here 400 years ago.

00:15:03.444 --> 00:15:05.279
We don't know its purpose

00:15:05.362 --> 00:15:07.948
but he would not
have left it lightly.

00:15:08.032 --> 00:15:10.659
The Latin inscription
translates as,

00:15:11.201 --> 00:15:14.246
"In the name of God,
open this door."

00:15:15.080 --> 00:15:16.874
There is an insignia.

00:15:21.086 --> 00:15:23.589
Yes, it matches your ring.

00:16:28.362 --> 00:16:29.947
No, Anna, it will kill you!

00:16:30.030 --> 00:16:31.573
That's my brother out there.

00:16:34.326 --> 00:16:36.537
Cut the rope! Cut it now!

00:16:50.300 --> 00:16:51.510
Velkan!

00:17:06.442 --> 00:17:07.568
Move.

00:17:09.403 --> 00:17:11.030
Anna, look out!

00:17:13.365 --> 00:17:14.533
Run!

00:17:44.646 --> 00:17:46.064
Velkan.

00:19:03.183 --> 00:19:04.768
What are we doing here?

00:19:04.852 --> 00:19:07.187
Why is it so important to
kill this Dracula, anyway?

00:19:07.271 --> 00:19:09.106
Because he's
the son of the Devil.

00:19:09.189 --> 00:19:10.274
I mean, besides that.

00:19:10.357 --> 00:19:13.694
If we kill him, anything bitten
or created by him will also die.

00:19:13.777 --> 00:19:14.778
I mean, besides that.

00:19:14.862 --> 00:19:17.656
Welcome to Transylvania.

00:19:29.877 --> 00:19:31.503
You, turn around.

00:19:37.050 --> 00:19:39.553
Gentlemen, you will
now be disarmed.

00:19:40.596 --> 00:19:42.014
You can try.

00:19:45.893 --> 00:19:48.061
You refuse to obey our laws?

00:19:48.270 --> 00:19:50.022
The laws of men
mean little to me.

00:20:05.954 --> 00:20:07.748
Hide the children!

00:20:31.313 --> 00:20:33.774
Carl, it's not working.

00:20:33.857 --> 00:20:36.026
Try aiming at their hearts.

00:21:39.423 --> 00:21:41.425
This should do the trick.

00:21:42.592 --> 00:21:44.136
Holy water!

00:21:49.725 --> 00:21:51.101
The church!

00:22:12.497 --> 00:22:14.041
Here she comes!

00:23:07.427 --> 00:23:08.637
He killed a bride!

00:23:08.720 --> 00:23:10.055
He killed Marishka!

00:23:14.768 --> 00:23:16.853
You killed Marishka!

00:23:17.396 --> 00:23:18.897
You killed a vampire!

00:23:18.980 --> 00:23:20.482
But isn't that a good thing?

00:23:20.565 --> 00:23:23.485
Vampires only kill what
they need to survive.

00:23:23.568 --> 00:23:25.612
One or two people a month.

00:23:26.154 --> 00:23:29.157
Now they will kill for revenge.

00:23:31.076 --> 00:23:35.997
So what name, my good sir, do
I carve on your gravestone?

00:23:36.081 --> 00:23:38.166
His name is Van Helsing.

00:23:44.673 --> 00:23:46.091
So, how did you get here?

00:23:46.174 --> 00:23:47.008
We came by sea.

00:23:47.092 --> 00:23:48.385
The Adriatic Sea?

00:23:48.468 --> 00:23:50.178
So, where do I find Dracula?

00:23:50.262 --> 00:23:53.265
He used to live in this
very house four centuries ago.

00:23:53.348 --> 00:23:55.308
No one knows
where he lives now.

00:23:55.392 --> 00:23:57.477
Father would stare at
that painting for hours

00:23:57.561 --> 00:23:59.229
looking for Dracula's lair.

00:23:59.312 --> 00:24:01.022
So that's why you've come?

00:24:01.106 --> 00:24:02.482
I can help you.

00:24:02.607 --> 00:24:04.151
The vampires
attacked in daylight.

00:24:04.234 --> 00:24:05.235
They never do that.

00:24:05.318 --> 00:24:07.696
I was unprepared.
It won't happen again.

00:24:07.779 --> 00:24:09.531
So why did they
attack in daylight?

00:24:09.614 --> 00:24:11.908
Clearly they wanted
to catch me off guard.

00:24:11.992 --> 00:24:14.286
They seem almost desperate
to finish off my family.

00:24:14.369 --> 00:24:16.204
Why is that? Why now?

00:24:16.288 --> 00:24:17.831
You ask a lot of questions.

00:24:17.914 --> 00:24:19.291
Usually I ask only two.

00:24:19.374 --> 00:24:21.209
What are we dealing with?
How do I kill it?

00:24:21.293 --> 00:24:22.627
My father spent
most of his life

00:24:22.711 --> 00:24:24.504
looking for
answers year after year.

00:24:25.046 --> 00:24:28.091
Tearing through the tower, combing
through the family archives.

00:24:28.175 --> 00:24:29.426
Carl, the tower. Start there.

00:24:29.509 --> 00:24:30.218
Right.

00:25:52.884 --> 00:25:54.010
Anna!

00:26:00.183 --> 00:26:01.893
Are you all right?

00:26:17.993 --> 00:26:19.202
Werewolf!

00:26:19.286 --> 00:26:21.288
Right. You'll be needing
silver bullets, then.

00:26:21.371 --> 00:26:22.747
Well done.

00:26:51.818 --> 00:26:52.986
Igor.

00:26:53.069 --> 00:26:54.487
Yes, Master.

00:26:54.571 --> 00:26:56.072
How long before we are ready?

00:26:56.156 --> 00:26:58.158
Soon, Master. Very soon.

00:26:59.618 --> 00:27:05.248
It is difficult without the good doctor
but the Dwergi, they are doing well?

00:27:05.332 --> 00:27:06.416
NO!

00:27:07.959 --> 00:27:09.085
Good.

00:27:21.639 --> 00:27:22.891
What is this place?

00:27:22.974 --> 00:27:24.809
Castle Frankenstein.

00:27:24.893 --> 00:27:26.728
But it should be abandoned.

00:27:26.811 --> 00:27:27.979
I don't understand.

00:27:28.063 --> 00:27:30.482
The man who lived here
was killed a year ago.

00:27:30.565 --> 00:27:31.900
A grave robber,
among other things.

00:27:31.983 --> 00:27:33.234
A year ago.

00:27:33.318 --> 00:27:35.737
It was just after that that
your father went missing.

00:27:35.820 --> 00:27:37.947
Yes. He was
looking for Dracula.

00:27:39.032 --> 00:27:41.117
I send you on a simple errand

00:27:41.201 --> 00:27:43.661
to find out who
our new visitor is

00:27:44.287 --> 00:27:47.749
and you have to stop for a
little chat with your sister.

00:27:47.832 --> 00:27:49.834
Leave her out of this, Count.

00:27:49.918 --> 00:27:51.878
She doesn't know your secret.

00:27:51.961 --> 00:27:54.381
And I am soon to
take it to my grave.

00:27:55.423 --> 00:27:57.092
Don't wish for
death so quickly.

00:27:57.175 --> 00:27:59.094
I intend for you
to be quite useful.

00:27:59.177 --> 00:28:00.929
I would rather
die than help you.

00:28:01.012 --> 00:28:02.180
Don't be boring.

00:28:02.263 --> 00:28:04.099
Everyone who says that dies.

00:28:04.182 --> 00:28:05.767
Besides, tonight,

00:28:05.850 --> 00:28:07.769
after the final
stroke of midnight,

00:28:07.852 --> 00:28:10.522
you will have no
choice but to obey me.

00:28:12.982 --> 00:28:14.526
Look familiar?

00:28:19.030 --> 00:28:20.198
Father?

00:28:20.865 --> 00:28:22.659
No!

00:28:22.867 --> 00:28:24.202
He proved useless.

00:28:24.285 --> 00:28:27.580
But I'm hoping, with werewolf
venom running through your veins

00:28:27.664 --> 00:28:29.624
you will be of greater benefit!

00:28:46.933 --> 00:28:47.934
Dwergi.

00:28:48.017 --> 00:28:49.144
Dwergi?

00:28:49.227 --> 00:28:50.728
Dracula's servants.

00:28:50.812 --> 00:28:52.814
Industrious but
extremely vicious.

00:28:59.612 --> 00:29:01.281
Let us begin!

00:29:10.373 --> 00:29:13.501
No slacking! Up!

00:29:28.391 --> 00:29:29.476
You ever
see these things before?

00:29:29.559 --> 00:29:30.560
NO.

00:29:30.643 --> 00:29:32.103
What do you think they are?

00:29:32.187 --> 00:29:33.354
Offspring.

00:29:33.438 --> 00:29:34.439
What?

00:29:34.522 --> 00:29:36.524
A man with three
gorgeous women for 400 years.

00:29:36.608 --> 00:29:39.360
Yes, vampires are
the walking dead.

00:29:39.444 --> 00:29:41.821
It only makes sense their
children are born dead.

00:29:41.905 --> 00:29:44.824
He's obviously trying
to bring them to life.

00:29:49.662 --> 00:29:51.164
Ladies first.

00:30:16.147 --> 00:30:19.859
Dracula and his brides only
kill one or two people a month.

00:30:20.276 --> 00:30:23.029
If he brings all these
things to life...

00:30:39.379 --> 00:30:40.755
Throw the switches!

00:30:40.839 --> 00:30:42.507
Yes, Master.

00:31:24.507 --> 00:31:25.717
Come on!

00:31:57.165 --> 00:31:59.083
They need to feed.

00:31:59.167 --> 00:32:01.294
Teach them how. Teach them!

00:32:08.885 --> 00:32:10.678
And beg the Devil

00:32:12.138 --> 00:32:14.599
that this time they stay alive.

00:32:33.951 --> 00:32:36.412
Now that I have your attention.

00:33:00.228 --> 00:33:02.480
Yes, well, that's interesting.

00:33:11.114 --> 00:33:12.573
That's not good.

00:33:30.758 --> 00:33:32.301
Hurry up!

00:33:34.387 --> 00:33:37.682
We must keep the
atmosphere electrified!

00:33:39.475 --> 00:33:41.644
Accelerate the generators!

00:33:42.603 --> 00:33:44.439
Power the dynamos!

00:33:45.648 --> 00:33:47.442
We are losing power.

00:33:48.484 --> 00:33:50.570
The human is insufficient.

00:33:53.322 --> 00:33:54.449
Velkan.

00:34:07.712 --> 00:34:09.088
Oh, my God.

00:34:40.620 --> 00:34:42.121
Hello, Gabriel.

00:34:50.296 --> 00:34:54.258
How long has it been?
300, 400 years?

00:34:59.514 --> 00:35:01.682
You don't remember, do you?

00:35:07.063 --> 00:35:11.818
We have such history,
you and I, Gabriel.

00:35:15.363 --> 00:35:21.410
Have you ever wondered why you
have such horrible nightmares?

00:35:21.494 --> 00:35:24.997
Horrific scenes of
ancient battles past.

00:35:29.460 --> 00:35:31.045
How do you know me?

00:35:38.886 --> 00:35:40.346
Velkan.

00:35:40.429 --> 00:35:42.098
Anna.

00:35:43.599 --> 00:35:47.562
Allow me to reintroduce myself.

00:35:48.229 --> 00:35:53.192
I am Count Vladislaus Dragulia.

00:35:55.111 --> 00:35:57.655
Born 1422.

00:35:58.781 --> 00:36:02.410
Murdered 1462.

00:36:27.560 --> 00:36:30.146
I think we've
overstayed our welcome.

00:37:16.734 --> 00:37:17.902
Have you found the children?

00:37:18.069 --> 00:37:19.278
Not yet.

00:37:22.657 --> 00:37:24.659
What happened?

00:37:24.742 --> 00:37:26.369
They just died.

00:37:27.078 --> 00:37:30.414
I am sorry, master.
We try and we try,

00:37:30.498 --> 00:37:35.044
but I fear we are not so smart as Dr.
Frankenstein.

00:37:35.795 --> 00:37:36.921
Truly.

00:37:38.130 --> 00:37:41.300
It would appear the good doctor
took the key to life to his grave.

00:37:44.720 --> 00:37:47.598
You were right. I'm sorry.

00:37:48.391 --> 00:37:50.559
He's not my brother anymore.

00:38:06.033 --> 00:38:07.493
Here's to what keeps you going.

00:38:07.576 --> 00:38:09.662
Absinthe. Strong stuff.

00:38:13.916 --> 00:38:17.336
Don't let it touch your tongue.
it'll knock you on your...

00:38:49.910 --> 00:38:52.079
There's something down here.

00:38:54.457 --> 00:38:56.334
And it's carnivorous.

00:38:59.503 --> 00:39:02.715
Whatever it is,
it appears to be human.

00:39:06.927 --> 00:39:11.599
I'd say he's a size 17.
Around 360 pounds.

00:39:12.433 --> 00:39:14.643
8.5 to 9 feet tall.

00:39:15.352 --> 00:39:19.732
He has a bad gimp in his right
leg and three copper teeth.

00:39:20.232 --> 00:39:21.359
Move!

00:39:26.864 --> 00:39:30.076
On, my God!
The Frankenstein monster!

00:39:32.286 --> 00:39:37.583
I have done nothing wrong and yet
you and your kind all wish me dead!

00:39:59.063 --> 00:40:00.731
What do you want?

00:40:24.588 --> 00:40:27.216
Oh, my God. He's seen us.

00:40:27.967 --> 00:40:29.426
Now they'll come for him.

00:40:29.510 --> 00:40:31.428
Neither you nor I will
be able to stop them.

00:40:31.512 --> 00:40:34.765
If I can get him to Rome,
we can protect him there.

00:40:34.849 --> 00:40:35.724
And then the painting came alive and
the two creatures attacked each other.

00:43:32.234 --> 00:43:32.860
Jump!

00:44:09.813 --> 00:44:10.814
Velkan.

00:44:18.697 --> 00:44:19.948
Anna.

00:44:27.373 --> 00:44:28.791
Forgive me.

00:44:37.424 --> 00:44:39.218
I will see you again.

00:44:50.479 --> 00:44:52.147
You killed him.

00:44:54.066 --> 00:44:56.694
Now you know why
they call me murderer.

00:45:04.952 --> 00:45:06.328
Oh, my God.

00:45:07.996 --> 00:45:09.790
You've been bitten.

00:45:37.693 --> 00:45:38.694
Anna.

00:46:03.552 --> 00:46:05.554
So much trouble to my master.

00:46:05.721 --> 00:46:07.765
So much trouble.

00:46:08.515 --> 00:46:09.600
What do you want?

00:46:09.683 --> 00:46:11.894
The master commands a trade.

00:46:13.937 --> 00:46:17.983
The monster for the Princess.

00:46:18.400 --> 00:46:20.903
Somewhere public.
Lots of people.

00:46:23.530 --> 00:46:25.324
A place where your master
will be less inclined

00:46:25.407 --> 00:46:27.701
to expose his other side.

00:46:30.412 --> 00:46:33.749
Tomorrow night is
All Hallows' Eve.

00:46:33.832 --> 00:46:38.587
Here in Budapest, there is
a wonderful masquerade ball.

00:46:49.765 --> 00:46:51.308
Are you all right?
No.

00:46:54.895 --> 00:46:56.396
He has been bitten.

00:46:56.480 --> 00:46:58.273
Bitten by a werewolf.

00:47:04.863 --> 00:47:06.240
I am sorry.

00:48:19.146 --> 00:48:20.439
There they are.

00:48:34.661 --> 00:48:36.955
Don't we make a lovely couple?

00:48:37.247 --> 00:48:38.707
Oh, my God.

00:48:38.790 --> 00:48:41.126
I am looking for
a new bride, Anna.

00:48:42.961 --> 00:48:45.464
Someone strong and beautiful.

00:49:24.711 --> 00:49:26.380
Anna. Anna!

00:49:26.755 --> 00:49:28.006
Wake up.

00:49:28.507 --> 00:49:29.758
Gabriel.

00:49:32.135 --> 00:49:34.054
Oh, Gabriel.

00:49:38.308 --> 00:49:40.602
Oh, Gabriel.

00:49:43.480 --> 00:49:46.358
Welcome to my summer palace.

00:49:47.109 --> 00:49:51.029
ladies and gentlemen,
I give to you,

00:49:52.614 --> 00:49:54.700
Van Helsing!

00:50:01.581 --> 00:50:03.542
Yes!

00:50:32.404 --> 00:50:34.740
Say goodbye to your friends.

00:50:54.760 --> 00:50:57.679
I'll find you!
I'll get you back and set you free!

00:50:57.763 --> 00:50:59.306
I swear to God!

00:51:07.230 --> 00:51:08.273
I must save him.

00:51:08.356 --> 00:51:10.817
No, you can't.
Why?

00:51:10.901 --> 00:51:13.195
I cabled Rome earlier to
apprise them of our situation.

00:51:13.278 --> 00:51:14.321
What did they say?

00:51:14.404 --> 00:51:15.614
Even if you
somehow kill Dracula,

00:51:15.697 --> 00:51:19.034
Rome orders you to destroy
Frankenstein as well.

00:51:19.117 --> 00:51:20.160
He isn't evil.

00:51:20.243 --> 00:51:22.037
But they say he
isn't human, either.

00:51:22.120 --> 00:51:23.663
Do they know him?
Have they spoken to him?

00:51:23.747 --> 00:51:24.790
Who are they to judge?

00:51:24.873 --> 00:51:27.918
They want you to destroy him so he
can never be used to harm humanity.

00:51:28.001 --> 00:51:30.337
What of me?
Did you tell them what I'm to become?

00:51:30.420 --> 00:51:32.297
Did they tell
you how to kill me?

00:51:32.380 --> 00:51:35.050
The correct angle of the
stake as it enters my heart?

00:51:35.133 --> 00:51:37.469
The exact measure of
silver in each bullet?

00:51:38.303 --> 00:51:39.471
Stop!

00:51:39.554 --> 00:51:40.680
No, I left you out!

00:51:59.282 --> 00:52:00.617
I'm sorry.

00:52:05.580 --> 00:52:07.040
It's starting.

00:52:21.721 --> 00:52:24.850
They must have taken all
the equipment to Dracula's lair.

00:52:25.642 --> 00:52:27.185
Wherever that is.

00:52:32.357 --> 00:52:34.025
Look, there's still time.

00:52:34.109 --> 00:52:36.736
Dracula can't bring his children
to life until the sun sets.

00:52:36.820 --> 00:52:38.071
The sun sets in two hours.

00:52:38.154 --> 00:52:40.073
We've been looking for him
for more than 400 years!

00:52:40.156 --> 00:52:43.827
Yes, well, I wasn't around for
those 400 years, now, was I?

00:52:45.162 --> 00:52:46.872
All right, Carl,
what have you learned?

00:52:46.955 --> 00:52:50.292
That Count Dracula was actually
the son of Valerious the Elder.

00:52:50.375 --> 00:52:51.751
The son of your ancestor.

00:52:51.835 --> 00:52:53.795
Everybody knows that.
What else?

00:52:53.879 --> 00:52:59.467
All right. Well, according to this rubbing
it all started when Dracula was murdered.

00:52:59.551 --> 00:53:00.844
Do you know who murdered him?
No,

00:53:00.927 --> 00:53:03.805
there's just some vague reference
to the Left Hand of God.

00:53:03.889 --> 00:53:07.976
And in 1462, when Dracula died,

00:53:08.059 --> 00:53:09.644
he made a covenant
with the Devil.

00:53:09.728 --> 00:53:11.271
And was given a new life.

00:53:11.354 --> 00:53:14.232
But the only way he could sustain
that life was by drinking blood.

00:53:14.316 --> 00:53:16.484
Excuse me. Are you going
to let me tell the story?

00:53:16.568 --> 00:53:17.569
Sorry.

00:53:17.652 --> 00:53:20.572
And your ancestor, having
sired this evil creature,

00:53:20.655 --> 00:53:23.074
went to Rome to
seek forgiveness.

00:53:23.158 --> 00:53:25.202
That's when the
bargain was made.

00:53:25.285 --> 00:53:26.453
He was to kill Dracula

00:53:26.536 --> 00:53:30.165
in return for eternal salvation
of his entire family

00:53:30.248 --> 00:53:32.542
right down the line
all the way to you.

00:53:32.626 --> 00:53:34.336
But he couldn't do it.

00:53:34.419 --> 00:53:37.005
As evil as Dracula was, my ancestor
couldn't kill his own son.

00:53:37.088 --> 00:53:40.675
So he banished him
to an icy fortress

00:53:40.759 --> 00:53:43.178
sending him through a door from
which there was no return.

00:53:43.261 --> 00:53:44.262
And then the Devil
gave him wings.

00:53:44.346 --> 00:53:45.347
Yes.

00:53:45.430 --> 00:53:46.932
All right,
so where is this door?

00:53:47.057 --> 00:53:48.600
I don't know.

00:53:49.809 --> 00:53:52.854
But when your ancestor couldn't
kill his son, he left clues.

00:53:54.814 --> 00:53:57.651
So that future generations
might do it for him.

00:53:57.734 --> 00:53:59.903
That must be what my father
was looking for in here.

00:53:59.986 --> 00:54:02.113
Clues to the door's location.

00:54:02.197 --> 00:54:03.531
The door.

00:54:06.159 --> 00:54:07.285
Of course.

00:54:08.620 --> 00:54:10.497
You said your father spent hours
staring at this painting,

00:54:10.580 --> 00:54:11.706
trying to find the lair.

00:54:11.790 --> 00:54:13.208
I think you were right.
Quite literally.

00:54:13.291 --> 00:54:17.128
I think this is the door.
He just didn't know how to open it.

00:54:17.212 --> 00:54:19.047
Look.
A Latin inscription.

00:54:19.130 --> 00:54:21.091
Maybe it works like that
painting in the tower.

00:54:21.174 --> 00:54:24.511
If this were a door, my father
would have opened it long ago.

00:54:25.595 --> 00:54:29.140
I can't finish the inscription.
There's a piece missing.

00:54:35.105 --> 00:54:36.398
Your father didn't have this.

00:54:36.481 --> 00:54:37.607
Where did you get that?

00:54:37.691 --> 00:54:39.317
Carl, finish it.

00:54:46.741 --> 00:54:49.536
In the name of God,
open this door.

00:55:01.840 --> 00:55:02.799
A mirror.

00:55:02.882 --> 00:55:04.134
But why?

00:55:26.990 --> 00:55:30.744
It's cold.
And it's snowing.

00:55:35.874 --> 00:55:37.917
See you on the other side.

00:56:14.579 --> 00:56:16.164
Castle Dracula.

00:56:52.826 --> 00:56:53.952
So are all of those...

00:56:54.035 --> 00:56:55.120
Yes.

00:56:55.203 --> 00:56:56.913
- And inside them are...
- Yes.

00:56:56.996 --> 00:56:59.999
Igor do this!
Igor do that!

00:57:02.377 --> 00:57:05.004
How did you find...
it's impossible!

00:57:10.009 --> 00:57:11.261
Please don't kill me!

00:57:11.344 --> 00:57:12.428
Why not?

00:57:13.471 --> 00:57:17.350
Now, if I'm not cured by the
twelfth stroke of midnight...

00:57:20.854 --> 00:57:22.063
I don't think I could.

00:57:22.147 --> 00:57:23.481
You must.

00:57:29.279 --> 00:57:30.530
Come on.

00:57:49.507 --> 00:57:53.052
What are you complaining about?
This is why you were made!

00:57:53.136 --> 00:57:57.223
To prove that God is not the
only one who can create life!

00:57:57.932 --> 00:58:02.103
And now you must give
that life to my children.

00:58:02.604 --> 00:58:03.646
Up!

00:59:16.177 --> 00:59:17.804
I'll go first.

00:59:40.159 --> 00:59:41.286
Carl!

00:59:43.955 --> 00:59:46.082
Stay as long as you like.

01:00:39.802 --> 01:00:41.471
Get it!

01:00:50.313 --> 01:00:50.897
Hot.

01:00:50.897 --> 01:00:51.898
Come on!
Yes.

01:00:55.234 --> 01:00:57.862
I'll say you can
go when you're dead!

01:01:40.446 --> 01:01:41.948
Oh, my God!

01:02:24.073 --> 01:02:26.242
Give me life!

01:02:41.549 --> 01:02:45.303
One more bolt and
my young will live.

01:02:58.983 --> 01:03:01.277
You're almost out, my friend!

01:04:49.135 --> 01:04:51.345
Hang on!

01:04:52.179 --> 01:04:54.515
I'll swing you loose!

01:05:23.127 --> 01:05:25.338
You are too late, my friend.

01:05:26.589 --> 01:05:28.341
My children live.

01:05:29.091 --> 01:05:32.094
Then the only way to
kill them is to kill you.

01:05:32.762 --> 01:05:33.888
Correct.

01:05:36.724 --> 01:05:38.059
So be it.

01:05:47.151 --> 01:05:49.946
No, this cannot be.

01:06:04.043 --> 01:06:07.588
We are both part of the
same grand game, Gabriel.

01:06:08.047 --> 01:06:11.926
But we need not find ourselves
on opposite sides of the board.

01:07:20.953 --> 01:07:22.788
Oh, my God!

01:07:35.885 --> 01:07:38.054
Throw it to me, Carl!

01:07:44.518 --> 01:07:45.519
Yes!

01:08:42.201 --> 01:08:46.413
Did I mention that it
was you who murdered me?

01:08:48.415 --> 01:08:51.043
All I want is life, Gabriel.

01:08:51.877 --> 01:08:54.088
The continuation of my kind.

01:08:54.755 --> 01:08:57.716
Don't be afraid, Gabriel.
Don't be afraid.

01:08:59.093 --> 01:09:04.348
I shall give you back
your life, your memory.

01:09:05.224 --> 01:09:07.476
Some things are
better left forgotten.

01:09:30.332 --> 01:09:31.584
For God!

01:09:40.718 --> 01:09:42.303
God forgive me.

01:11:03.092 --> 01:11:04.843
"Eternal rest grant unto her,

01:11:04.927 --> 01:11:06.345
"Oh, Lord,
and let perpetual light

01:11:06.428 --> 01:11:08.847
”shine upon her.
On her soul and the souls of all

01:11:16.689 --> 01:11:18.482
”On her soul and
the souls of all

01:11:18.565 --> 01:11:22.152
"the dead
faithful have mercy.”
